// Recover the implicit-domain `count` via the explicit form:
//   count for (t: Timepoint). where formerly within 1h (Withdraw(_) ∧ tp(t))
//
// Project onto the timepoint binder `t` and count distinct rows: the
// number of past timepoints (within 1h) at which a Transfer occurred,
// regardless of who or how much. `tp(t)` binds `t` to each visited
// timepoint so the rows stay one-per-timepoint.
//
// Trace (decision at the Alert, ts=3700; window 1h = 3600s): Transfers
// at ts=0, 100, 200, 3600 (the last one second before the decision, the
// strictly-monotone stand-in for a same-instant event). ts=0 is out of
// window (3700-0 = 3700 > 3600); the other three are in → count = 3.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). ((count for (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.amount: * } && tp(t)))) == n && n == 3)};
